This is the **agent_bootstrap** repo — the source of truth for all AI agent configurations deployed across workspaces.

## Repo layout

- `skills/` — 35+ skill definitions (each has a SKILL.md)
- `rules/` — Cursor rule files (.mdc)
- `mcp/` — MCP server configs and docs
- `agents/` — Subagent definitions
- `commands/` — Command/prompt templates
- `hooks/` — Lifecycle hook scripts
- `manifest.json` — Tracks source plugin hashes, sync state, and MCP provenance (v2)
- `install.sh` — Interactive plugin manager + deployment tool (replaces old sync.sh)
- `.local-config` — Per-machine plugin selections (gitignored)

## When the user asks to update or sync this repo

Run `./install.sh` and use the interactive menu:
1. **Option 1: Update** — pulls latest from GitHub (`git fetch && git pull`)
2. **Option 2: Initialize** — discovers all plugins (repo, cache, local), shows dual-checkbox menu for Repo/Local selection, confirms changes, syncs everything

The Initialize flow handles all of:
- Pulling new/updated plugins from Cursor cache into the repo
- Removing deselected plugins from the repo (skills, rules, agents, commands, hooks, MCP)
- Deploying/removing local configs (MCP servers, Codex skills, workspace rules)
- Regenerating skill catalogs for all tracked workspaces
- Offering git commit + push when repo files change

## When the user asks to install or set up

### Interactive (recommended)
- `./install.sh` — launches the plugin manager menu

### Scripted / CI
- `./install.sh --global` — global MCP, Codex skills, env var
- `./install.sh --all ~/ATOM/` — all repos under ATOM
- `./install.sh --workspace <path>` — single repo
- `./install.sh --status` — show what's configured

These commands respect `.local-config` if present (created by the interactive menu).

## Available skills in this repo

You can read any skill at `skills/*/SKILL.md` to learn how to perform specialized tasks.
